@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-d-common-source`

-- ===========================================================================
-- s 66(a).  Lines 2455-2458.
--
--   (א) על אף האמור בסעיף 65 –
--   (1) רשאי בן זוג שאיננו בן זוג רשום לתבוע כי ייעשה חישוב נפרד של המס על
--       הכנסתו מיגיעה אישית בעסק או משלח יד או מעבודה, לרבות הכנסתו מיגיעה
--       אישית כאמור בפסקאות (1) עד (7) להגדרתה שבסעיף 1, ובלבד שלגבי הכנסה
--       כאמור שהיא קיצבה ייעשה חישוב נפרד אם היא משולמת בשל הכנסת עבודה
--       שלגביה היה בן הזוג שאיננו בן הזוג הרשום זכאי לחישוב נפרד, או אם בן
--       הזוג שאיננו בן הזוג הרשום היה זכאי בחמש השנים האחרונות שלפני תחילת
--       תשלום הקיצבה לחישוב נפרד בשל ההכנסה שמכוחה משתלמת הקיצבה;
--   (2) לענין חישוב המס תיווסף ההכנסה החייבת שאינה מיגיעה אישית של בני הזוג
--       להכנסה החייבת של בן הזוג שהכנסתו החייבת מיגיעה אישית גבוהה יותר; לא
--       היתה לבני הזוג הכנסה חייבת מיגיעה אישית, יראו את ההכנסה שאינה מיגיעה
--       אישית כהכנסת בן הזוג הרשום;
--   (3) לענין הכנסות מחברה שקופה כהגדרתה בסעיף 64א1, הכנסות מקרן להשקעות
--       במקרקעין, כהגדרתה בסעיף 64א2, והכנסות מריבית או מריווח הון, יראו את
--       הכנסותיו של בן הזוג הרשום ככוללות גם הכנסות כאמור של ילדו שטרם מלאו
--       לו בשנת המס 18 שנים; לענין סעיף זה, ”ריבית“ – כמשמעותה בסעיף 65.
--
-- "על אף האמור בסעיף 65": s 65 (outside this slice) puts the whole income of
-- the spouses on the registered spouse.  Subsection (a) displaces it where a
-- separate calculation is made; the displacement is written as the arm order
-- of `the calculations under subsections (a) and (b)` in
-- ito66-ab-taxable-income.l4, where the (a) arm is asked first.
--
-- Subsection (a) as a whole is gated by subsection (d); see
-- ito66-d-common-source.l4.
--
-- TAX YEARS (version 0.2.0, 02-V4).  Every rule here that takes the couple,
-- and so carries the tax year, asks `in tax year … , the answer is` first and
-- refuses a year before 2024 (assumption A1, ito66-tax-years.l4).  The rules
-- that take one spouse or one item carry no year and state the deposited
-- text; so do the two accessors under "Which spouse is meant", which are
-- plumbing, not law.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Which spouse is meant`

-- Plumbing, not law: the record of the spouse a `Which spouse` names, and of
-- the other one.
GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`the particulars of the` which `in` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `registered spouse`                       THEN couple's `the registered spouse`
    WHEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse` THEN couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`

GIVEN which  IS A `Which spouse`
      couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`the particulars of the partner of the` which `in` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER which
    WHEN `registered spouse`                       THEN couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
    WHEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse` THEN couple's `the registered spouse`

§ `Section 66(a)(1) — the claim of the spouse who is not the registered spouse`

-- "קיצבה".  Of the eight paragraphs of the s 1 definition that (a)(1) brings
-- in, five are pensions by their own words: (1), (2), (3), (3A) and (4).  (5)
-- is a grant, (6) a sum received on commuting a pension, (7) rent.  Reading
-- (fork F2): a commuted sum under (6) is not itself a "קיצבה", so the proviso
-- does not reach it.
@ref s 1, definition of "הכנסה מיגיעה אישית", paras (1)-(4) and (3A), lines 171-175
GIVEN k IS A `Kind of income from personal exertion`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a pension` k MEANS
        k EQUALS `a pension paid by a former employer`
    OR  k EQUALS `a pension from a pension provident fund`
    OR  k EQUALS `a pension paid to the survivors of a person within paragraph (1) or (2)`
    OR  k EQUALS `a pension for loss of working capacity`
    OR  k EQUALS `a taxable pension paid by the National Insurance Institute`

-- The proviso ("ובלבד ש..."): a pension is calculated separately only on one
-- of its two conditions.  Every other kind of income from personal exertion
-- is within (a)(1) without condition.
--
-- Both conditions are BOOLEAN facts on the item (version 0.2.0, 02-X2): the
-- edge of the second, "בחמש השנים האחרונות שלפני תחילת תשלום הקיצבה", is not
-- computed from dates here, so whether an entitlement fell within the five
-- years is the caller's to decide (NOTES.md section 1).
@ref s 66(a)(1), proviso, line 2456
GIVEN `the item` IS AN `An item of income from personal exertion`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` `the item` MEANS
        NOT `a pension` (`the item`'s `kind`)
    OR  `the item`'s `paid in respect of employment income for which the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation`
    OR  `the item`'s `the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation, in the five years before the pension began, for the income by virtue of which it is paid`

@ref s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 1 definition of "הכנסה מיגיעה אישית", line 170
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income from personal exertion of` `the spouse` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD i's `taxable amount`) (`the spouse`'s `income from personal exertion`))

@ref s 66(a)(1), line 2456
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may be calculated separately, of` `the spouse` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD IF   `s 66(a)(1) — may be calculated separately:` i
                            THEN i's `taxable amount`
                            ELSE 0)
             (`the spouse`'s `income from personal exertion`))

-- The income from personal exertion that the proviso keeps out of the
-- separate calculation.  Nothing in s 66 moves it, so it stays where s 65
-- puts it: on the registered spouse.
@ref s 66(a)(1), proviso, line 2456; s 65, line 2448
GIVEN `the spouse` IS A `A spouse`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may not be calculated separately, of` `the spouse` MEANS
        `the taxable income from personal exertion of` `the spouse`
    MINUS `s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may be calculated separately, of` `the spouse`

-- "רשאי ... לתבוע": an entitlement, so a BOOLEAN.  Subsection (d) gates it.
-- Version 0.4.0 (fork F1, ito66-d-common-source.l4).  Where a common source
-- fails (d)(1): under (i) no claim lies; under (ii) the claim lies on the
-- income within (a)(1) that does not come from the source; and by default
-- the claim is declined where those differ, which is wherever (ii) leaves
-- something to calculate separately, or the facts do not say how much comes
-- from the source.  Where neither reading leaves anything, both say no.
@ref s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 66(d)(1), line 2479; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F1
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (IF   `s 66(d)(1) — the spouses have no common source of income, or one that meets every condition:` couple
         THEN `within (a)(1)` GREATER THAN 0
         ELSE CONSIDER `the reading of section 66(d)(1) taken for` couple
              WHEN `subsection (a) does not apply to the spouses at all`
                  THEN FALSE
              WHEN `subsection (a) does not apply to the income from the common source alone`
                  THEN `within (a)(1)` MINUS `from the source` GREATER THAN 0
              WHEN `declined where the readings of section 66(d)(1) differ`
                  THEN BRANCH
                           IF   `within (a)(1)` EQUALS 0
                           THEN FALSE
                           IF   `s 66(d)(1) — the facts give the income of the spouse who is not the registered spouse from a common source that fails, for` couple
                                AND `within (a)(1)` MINUS `from the source` AT MOST 0
                           THEN FALSE
                           OTHERWISE `section 66(d)(1) does not say whether a common source of income that fails its conditions keeps subsection (a) from the spouses or only from the income of that source`)
    WHERE
        `within (a)(1)`   MEANS `s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may be calculated separately, of`
                                    (couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`)
        `from the source` MEANS `s 66(d)(1) — the income from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse from a common source that fails, for` couple

-- Fork F1, reading (ii): the income from a failing common source that a
-- separate calculation under (a)(1) leaves out.  It stays where s 65 puts it,
-- on the registered spouse.  0 wherever no separate calculation is made, and
-- wherever the source passes or there is none.
@ref s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 66(d)(1), line 2479; s 65, line 2448; fork F1
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(1) with (d)(1) — the income from a failing common source kept out of the separate calculation, for` couple MEANS
    IF   `s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` couple
         AND NOT `s 66(d)(1) — the spouses have no common source of income, or one that meets every condition:` couple
    THEN min (`s 66(d)(1) — the income from personal exertion of the spouse who is not the registered spouse from a common source that fails, for` couple)
             (`s 66(a)(1) — the income from personal exertion that may be calculated separately, of` (couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`))
    ELSE 0

@ref s 66(a)(1), line 2456; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(a)(1) — a separate calculation is made, for` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (    `s 66(a)(1) — the spouse who is not the registered spouse may claim a separate calculation, for` couple
         AND couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`'s `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion`)

§ `Section 66(a)(2) — the income not from personal exertion`

-- READING (fork F4): "בן הזוג שהכנסתו החייבת מיגיעה אישית גבוהה יותר" is
-- compared on each spouse's whole taxable income from personal exertion,
-- including any pension the (a)(1) proviso keeps out of the separate
-- calculation.
--
-- The first sentence picks the spouse with the HIGHER income; the second
-- covers spouses with none.  Spouses with EQUAL, non-zero income from
-- personal exertion are answered by neither sentence (fork F3), and the rule
-- refuses rather than choosing one.  The arms are disjoint and in the
-- source's order.
@ref s 66(a)(2), line 2457
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 66(a)(2) does not say which spouse takes the income not from personal exertion where their incomes from personal exertion are equal` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 66(a)(2) does not say which spouse takes the income not from personal exertion where their incomes from personal exertion are equal"

@ref s 66(a)(2), line 2457; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `Which spouse`
`s 66(a)(2) — the spouse to whose taxable income the income not from personal exertion is added, for` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (BRANCH
            IF   `registered` GREATER THAN `other`
            THEN `registered spouse`
            IF   `other` GREATER THAN `registered`
            THEN `spouse who is not the registered spouse`
            IF   `registered` EQUALS 0 AND `other` EQUALS 0
            THEN `registered spouse`
            OTHERWISE `s 66(a)(2) does not say which spouse takes the income not from personal exertion where their incomes from personal exertion are equal`)
    WHERE
        `registered` MEANS `the taxable income from personal exertion of` (couple's `the registered spouse`)
        `other`      MEANS `the taxable income from personal exertion of` (couple's `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`)

§ `Section 66(a)(3) — the income of a child under 18`

-- "ילדו שטרם מלאו לו בשנת המס 18 שנים": a child of the registered spouse who
-- has not turned 18 by the end of the tax year, so whose age in the tax year
-- (tax year less tax year of birth) is at most 17.  A child born after the
-- tax year is not yet a child in it.
--
-- READINGS (forks F5, F6): "ילדו" is the registered spouse's own child, so a
-- child of the other spouse alone is not reached; and (a)(3), unlike s 65,
-- states no exception for assets received by inheritance or from personal
-- injury compensation, so none is applied.  (Version 0.4.0: F6 is now a
-- switch, below, applied to the children's income as a whole; whether a
-- child is within (a)(3) does not turn on it.)
@ref s 66(a)(3), line 2458; s 66 amendment list, line 2454
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
      `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 66(a)(3) — for` couple `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` `the child` MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (    `the child`'s `a child of the registered spouse`
         AND couple's `tax year` AT LEAST `the child`'s `tax year of birth`
         AND couple's `tax year` MINUS `the child`'s `tax year of birth` LESS THAN 18)

-- "הכנסות מחברה שקופה ... מקרן להשקעות במקרקעין ... מריבית או מריווח הון".
@ref s 66(a)(3), line 2458
GIVEN `the child` IS A `A child, for section 66`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(3) — the income within the paragraph, of` `the child` MEANS
         `the child`'s `taxable income from a transparent company`
    PLUS `the child`'s `taxable income from a real estate investment trust`
    PLUS `the child`'s `taxable income from interest`
    PLUS `the child`'s `taxable income from capital gain`

-- FORK F6 (version 0.4.0; RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG; inventory
-- 02-F6).  s 65, line 2448, keeps a child's income from interest, a real
-- estate investment trust or capital gain off the registered spouse "אלא אם
-- כן הנכסים שמהם היתה ההכנסה ... התקבלו בירושה, או שמקורם בפיצויים או בכספי
-- ביטוח שהתקבלו בשל פגיעת גוף".  (a)(3) restates s 65's child rule without
-- that exception and borrows only s 65's meaning of "ריבית".  (i) No exception
-- under (a)(3) (the reading of 0.1.0-0.3.0); (ii) the exception travels with
-- the rule.  The default declines where the children have such income.
@ref s 66(a)(3), line 2458; s 65, line 2448; fork F6; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) as to the exception in section 65`
`section 66(a)(3) — the reading this row takes of the exception in section 65` MEANS
    `declined where the readings of the exception in section 65 differ`

@ref s 66(a)(3), line 2458; s 65, line 2448; fork F6
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 66(a)(3) does not say whether section 65's exception for assets received by inheritance or from compensation for bodily injury applies under it` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 66(a)(3) does not say whether section 65's exception for assets received by inheritance or from compensation for bodily injury applies under it"

GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) as to the exception in section 65`
`the reading of the exception in section 65 taken for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `section 66(a)(3) — the reading this row takes of the exception in section 65`
    WHEN JUST rs THEN rs's `F6, the exception in section 65 under (a)(3)`

-- Version 0.2.0 (02-V4): gated as well as the per-child rule above, so that
-- a couple with no children is refused for a year before 2024 too.
-- Version 0.4.0 (F6): under (ii) the part from inherited or compensation
-- assets (an input on the couple) is not the registered spouse's; the default
-- declines where there is such a part and income for it to come out of.
@ref s 66(a)(3), line 2458; s 65, line 2448; s 66 amendment list, line 2454; fork F6
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` couple MEANS
    `in tax year` (couple's `tax year`) `, the answer is`
        (CONSIDER `the reading of the exception in section 65 taken for` couple
         WHEN `section 65's exception does not apply under (a)(3)` THEN `the sum`
         WHEN `section 65's exception applies under (a)(3)`        THEN max 0 (`the sum` MINUS `the part`)
         WHEN `declined where the readings of the exception in section 65 differ`
             THEN IF   `the part` EQUALS 0 OR `the sum` EQUALS 0
                  THEN `the sum`
                  ELSE `section 66(a)(3) does not say whether section 65's exception for assets received by inheritance or from compensation for bodily injury applies under it`)
    WHERE
        `the sum`  MEANS sum (map (GIVEN c YIELD IF   `s 66(a)(3) — for` couple `, the income of this child is the registered spouse's:` c
                                                 THEN `s 66(a)(3) — the income within the paragraph, of` c
                                                 ELSE 0)
                                  (couple's `children`))
        `the part` MEANS couple's `of the children's income within (a)(3), the part from assets received by inheritance or from compensation or insurance for bodily injury`

-- FORK F14 (version 0.4.0; RULED by Meng on 2026-10-08, SHRUG; inventory
-- 02-F6, which names it with F6).  (a)(3) deems the children's income the
-- registered spouse's; (a)(2) sends "ההכנסה החייבת שאינה מיגיעה אישית של בני
-- הזוג" to the spouse with the higher income from personal exertion.  (i) The
-- children's income stays with the registered spouse, (a)(3) naming him (the
-- reading of 0.1.0-0.3.0); (ii) once his, it is income not from personal
-- exertion of the spouses and goes with the pool.  They differ only where the
-- pool goes to the spouse who is not the registered spouse and there is such
-- income; the default declines there.
@ref s 66(a)(2), (a)(3), lines 2457-2458; fork F14; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-08 (SHRUG)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) where (a)(2) sends the pooled income to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
`section 66(a)(2)-(3) — the reading this row takes of the children's income when the pool goes to the spouse who is not the registered spouse` MEANS
    `declined where the readings of the children's income and the pool differ`

@ref s 66(a)(2), (a)(3), lines 2457-2458; fork F14
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 66 does not say whether the children's income that (a)(3) deems the registered spouse's goes with the income (a)(2) sends to the other spouse` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 66 does not say whether the children's income that (a)(3) deems the registered spouse's goes with the income (a)(2) sends to the other spouse"

GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A `A reading of section 66(a)(3) where (a)(2) sends the pooled income to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
`the reading of the children's income and the pool taken for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER couple's `the readings of section 66 to take, if not this row's`
    WHEN NOTHING  THEN `section 66(a)(2)-(3) — the reading this row takes of the children's income when the pool goes to the spouse who is not the registered spouse`
    WHEN JUST rs THEN rs's `F14, the children's income under (a)(3) when the pool goes to the other spouse`

-- The children's income that goes with the pool to the spouse who is not
-- the registered spouse; asked only where (a)(2) sends it there.
@ref s 66(a)(2), (a)(3), lines 2457-2458; fork F14
GIVEN couple IS A `Spouses in a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 66(a)(2)-(3) — the children's income that goes with the pool to the spouse who is not the registered spouse, for` couple MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reading of the children's income and the pool taken for` couple
    WHEN `the children's income stays with the registered spouse` THEN 0
    WHEN `the children's income goes with the pooled income`      THEN `the children's income`
    WHEN `declined where the readings of the children's income and the pool differ`
        THEN IF   `the children's income` EQUALS 0
             THEN 0
             ELSE `section 66 does not say whether the children's income that (a)(3) deems the registered spouse's goes with the income (a)(2) sends to the other spouse`
    WHERE
        `the children's income` MEANS `s 66(a)(3) — the children's income deemed the registered spouse's, for` couple
